  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RESCUE: response for evidence-driven scaling of emergency shelter and non-food items in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya is one of the top countries affected by, and at continued risk for, the devastating effects of climate change. Kenya also hosts two of among the world&#x2019;s most populous refugee camps and contain resident populations in need of distinct humanitarian support in its Arid and Semi-Arid Lands (ASALs). Despite Kenya&#x2019;s propensity for natural hazards, the Country&#x2019;s poor disaster preparedness planning and lack of comprehensive early warning systems have left the affected populations unprepared for dramatic climate-driven disasters. This Action contributes to preserving life and enhancing living conditions of shock-affected and displaced populations in Kenya. Through this project, IOM is providing evidence-driven, anticipatory, and targeted shelter and settlements support to people on the move, as well as host and pastoralist communities in ASALs.</narrative>
  </description>
